DEPENDENCY REDISTRIBUTION TEXTS

internal/packaging/assets/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES contains original complete license,
copyright and upstream NOTICE texts collected deterministically from pinned
Go product-package dependencies, the Go standard library/toolchain, non-dev npm
lock dependencies, copied UI/font sources and keysym sources. Each original file
has its package/version identity, source reference and SHA-256. It conservatively
includes a dependency graph rather than claiming linker-level reachability.
Regenerate the text bundle and authoritative LICENSE/NOTICE asset copies with
node test/tooling/generate-license-notices.mjs after pinned dependencies are
installed and web assets exist. Initial collection may take an explicit audited
Go product-module list as its sole argument. Version-pinned upstream legal files
omitted by some npm publications are retained, with immutable source URLs, in
test/tooling/upstream-license-texts.json; this is not a generic inferred grant.
Native packages install LICENSE, NOTICE and THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES under their
/usr/share/doc/<product>/ directory; OCI and release exports retain these texts.
Build tools, operating-system runtime packages and operator-supplied CA bundles
retain their own licenses and redistribution requirements.
